| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 secret lifetime | The core binds disclosure to the review: each applied change records the review it came from, and `DiscardChange` on an applied review forgets every one-time key its changes returned, settled or not; a forget on an unsettled change marks it so the key is dropped the moment it lands (`forget_on_settle`), never held. The review sheet ends every review it opened on each exit: Done, Escape, the scrim, Finish later, and unmount (navigation, tenant switch, window close), the last deferred one tick so a development re-mount cancels it. Tests: `ui_v2_reviews::a_key_that_lands_after_the_review_closed_is_dropped_on_arrival` (delayed issuance, review left while the write is on the wire, result `forgotten`, rotation `resumed`, Reveal refused, nothing shown), `leaving_an_applied_review_retires_its_held_key`, and `administration.test.tsx` "a review exit ends the review in the core, also before its change settles and on unmount" | `change_domain.rs`, `review-sheet.tsx` |
| R2 reconciliation evidence | An unconfirmed issuance keeps the key name its review named (`Rotation.pending_name`); only a key of that application with that exact name, and not the old key, confirms it. Absence is established only by the whole inventory in one read (a first page that is also the last), or by a key detail read, which walks the whole inventory (its `absent` is authoritative). Tests: `a_failed_or_unknown_issuance_claims_nothing_until_a_key_is_read_back` (an unrelated key of the application leaves it unconfirmed), `a_rejected_or_unknown_removal_keeps_the_reminder_until_the_key_is_read_back_gone` (a non-first final page without the old key completes nothing), `a_key_detail_walk_reconciles_an_unconfirmed_removal` | `rotation_domain.rs`, `management_domain.rs` |
| R3 issuedBy vs validator | Acknowledging the deployment forgets the held key (the operator states the application has it); `issuedBy` is emitted only while the key is held and the stage may reveal it (`issued`, `issuanceUnconfirmed`), and the TypeScript validator admits exactly those stages. Test: `acknowledging_the_deployment_forgets_the_held_key` | `rotation_domain.rs`, `client.ts` |
| R4 completed Version without a found readback | Any sent Version (completed or unknown) whose readback did not find the key is an explicit `issuanceUnconfirmed` rotation with the held key still revealable once and a reconciliation path (the reviewed name); nothing is reissued. A refused Version shows the core's result as an alert. Test: `a_completed_version_whose_readback_missed_is_an_unconfirmed_issuance` | `rotation_domain.rs`, `review-sheet.tsx`, `rotation-panel.tsx` |
| R5 applied success not action-specific | `appliedState`: a delete is removed only when completed without failure and read back absent; any other action is live only when completed without failure and read back found; unknown or completed-with-failure is unconfirmed; anything else failed. Reconciliation reads the reviewed item itself (its detail by ID, or the inventory by name for a creation; Gateway kinds through the workspace's Gateway read) and shows what that read established. Toasts confirm completions for the tenant they belong to | `review-sheet.tsx` (tests in `administration.test.tsx`) |
| R6 per-tab contracts, Gateway review, inventory-driven actions | Red Team tabs render their own read surface (Overview tiles and window, Targets, Scans, Attack results, Reports); model tabs render Overview, Model scans or Skill scans. Gateway changes open the shell's review sheet with typed confirmation and secret disposal, keeping the draft hook and note; Gateway create, row and workspace actions and labels come from the inventory. Runtime create and row actions are exactly the tab's admitted actions in the inventory's order | `red-team-view.tsx`, `gateway-view.tsx`, `administration-view.tsx`, `administration.tsx` |
| R7 relationships and key state | One walk of a profile's policy (`topicRefs`) gives the Security profiles "Topics" column and, over one profiles read, the Custom topics "Used by" column ("None in the profiles read" when that read was not the whole inventory). The key table has a State column ("Replace after deployment" for the old key, "New key for <application>" for the new one) and re-reads its page (and an open detail) when a change of its kind settles or a rotation moves on | `administration-view.tsx` |
| R8 response topic results | `ScanResultView.responseTopics` from `response_detected.topic_violation` and `response_detection_details.topic_guardrails_details`; the Playground shows "Custom topics · prompt" and "Custom topics · response" separately | `scanning.rs`, `runtime-view.tsx`, `client.ts` |
| R9 live region | The rotation panel has one persistent polite status region announcing each observed stage change for the tenant it opened for; a stage change that removes the focused control keeps focus in the panel | `rotation-panel.tsx` |
| E2 coverage | `administration.test.tsx`: V2-T20 walks every product and tab of the inventory (disposition, content, exactly the admitted creation and row actions, in order); Gateway key rows with Rotate in place through the typed review; V2-T21 (a reply's target name never renders; `red_team::a_target_name_never_reaches_the_targets_scope` in the core); review exit and pending settlement; R5, R7, R8, R9 | tests |
| E3 native | C31-N04 adds the review sheet's focus ring (pixel diff against the unfocused capture), the applied result and rotation completion in status regions, and the applied toast persisting under Reduce Motion until dismissed (setting restored) | `acceptance_c31.py`, `native-checks.json` |

